nodecode-wikipedia is a rewrite of EloquentBrush0x's EloquentBrush0x/hermes-context-refs:

  https://github.com/EloquentBrush0x/hermes-context-refs
  commit 0154f6bfaafc837cc4af78742e6db7c087d5b5a7
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 EloquentBrush0x (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's `wiki-ref` folder, whose `@wiki:<title>` context
reference becomes a Nodecode tool (`wikipedia`) and a slash command (`/wiki`).
The MediaWiki query, the trailer that marks the text as quoted material, the
section walk over the plain-text extract (one section plus its subsections,
exact heading before a case-insensitive one), the pronunciation clean-up, the
word-boundary truncation, the edition/max_chars/timeout settings and the "did
you mean" suggestions on a miss are the original's, reimplemented in Common
Lisp against the cell contract.

Left out: Hermes's `@prefix:` reference syntax and its keystroke autocomplete,
which are that harness's own; the same two shapes live here as a tool argument
and a `Title#Section` target, and a miss answers with the titles or headings
that would have autocompleted. Also left out: the same-host redirect guard, since
the cell hands redirects to Nodecode's own HTTP client, which bounds how many it
follows instead of checking the host here.
